			"notes": "- Click anywhere on the map to see its biome, what it is made of and how high it is, with buttons to copy its coordinates, a /tp command or a link, and the matching spot in the Nether or overworld.\n- The address bar holds where you are looking, so a link opens on the same spot; a search box finds players, homes, villages, portals, signs, beacons, shared places and deaths, or goes to typed coordinates; a ruler measures distances.\n- New layers: signs whose first line is [map], beacons with their effects and reach, places shared in TP Me Plz, where players died, the world border, night darkening the overworld, and the caves under the surface.\n- Sky builds such as cloud kingdoms can be hidden to see the ground under them.\n- Players show as their faces and glide between updates. For privacy they are shown 30 seconds late, and not at all while sneaking or deep underground.\n- Ops can hide an area from the map with /webmap hide; it looks like map nobody has explored.\n- Pinching on a phone zooms the map rather than the page.\n- The saved world is drawn once more, at low priority, so these details reach what was drawn before."
		},
